        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_513c2d18c1e648c1b8d269e28bd3816d",
      "statement": "Under LDI-2012-05, a hurricane deductible applicable to windstorm and hail losses could not exceed 5% of insured value, and the notice had to state the calculation basis and match the policy deductible.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L47-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f535d7f5052fb4c0745bf051b7f199ddbb2c75df2b15ea30f6bc1505579c9e64:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ef1f808fca904b30adaefa88ef2f8d38",
      "statement": "LDI-2012-05 required the deductible disclosure before an applicant became obligated under the policy and before renewal when the renewed policy contained the deductible; it required clear separation from other deductibles and permitted delivery through application, declarations, endorsement, renewal offer, or separate communication.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L49-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1b4256dc97a3d4bfcdf271628bad9181d2765b48140bb5213002bcf8a489287a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L71-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7713b7afd8afa8e33b5c7ee379d0ad4311373c2fbb157d38a81239ddc6c54d4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L89-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb51ca1bfb0ff12928cd62f7b888c9236ffa365070c9db8c0b3a3700bf92f200:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_003a072e2a09446ea18273a7f94522b0",
      "statement": "LDI-2012-05 did not prescribe a fixed named-storm duration or 72-hour continuation; instead, it required the notice to explain whether the hurricane deductible depended on a hurricane declaration or designation by an authorized governmental authority and to identify the applicable event or condition.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L55-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b3fcc3ebc36685db349d49befdedb7b7355f095d40e30956347b5fffdb7af2b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b2caf697f4c046a98188fb0a21022202",
      "statement": "LDI-2012-05 required at least 30 days' written notice before an increase in a windstorm deductible, prohibited making the increase effective without notice, and required Department filing and approval of the notice before use, with material revisions filed before use.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L153-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9819b96c5e6c17ae669b22a3215885449414ca63586ca59409ea55304c091ad7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L257-L273",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b067493db990b27ba8793849a779471c5cad3f6d234de661e432f1da7066a655:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_02eec971ce9741bbb0f5f94e36a37bae",
      "statement": "LDI-2012-05 required prompt claim investigation and a policy-based deductible determination, documentation distinguishing hurricane-deductible damage from other damage, written explanations of payments or denials reflecting the deductible, no delay to undisputed portions, preservation of material claim records, and correction of erroneous deductible determinations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2012-05-hurricane-deductible.md#L215-L251",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c7f8176aeef804b2830576aa574f431fb8416388c732df62ebba904db3c0e78:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ba35740481c74a418fa312c29d5b57ce",
      "statement": "LDI-2020-07 requires hurricane deductibles and named-storm periods to be administered consistently with the policy contract, states a 5% maximum of applicable covered loss, and requires disclosure of the percentage calculation basis.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2020-07-hurricane-deductible.md#L59-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef1af59eba66e3c8a0583c79c6c99a29e0037fca739a0f4dd9fffcb6f3d66950:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aa959dddbd6a44b182fa4f71d6ac653a",
      "statement": "Under the 2020 Louisiana regime implemented by HO 01 17, the Named Storm Period begins when the named-storm designation takes effect and continues for 72 hours after it ends; the insurer determines designation and loss timing from reliable information and the facts, not from the discovery date alone.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/LA/ldi-2020-07-hurricane-deductible.md#L199-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:973ab782e02a84e63b3b67c2370e2b2bc1e3cca679a8358f5481c93fc6ef2dda:"
        },
        {
